# Fixed 2026-09-30, defect 131's class, lane recovery-b4, beside
# `fixedbugs-131-a-sigil-before-a-name-is-one-message`. Symptom: an `@` at a
# statement's start before anything but a name, `@ 5` or `@1`, cost
# `expected_expression` and then `not_a_place` at the one token: the place
# the `@` needs is left out, and the place that could not be read was named
# no place, a second message for the one mistake. It is told once now, by
# what refused it, and the value after the `@` is still read, so its own
# mistake is told.

function main()
    v: i64 @= 0
    @ 5  #~ expected_expression
    @1  #~ expected_expression
    @ 5 + )  #~ expected_expression expected_expression
    print(v)
